OS HUMANOS,\" also known as the Convention for the Protection of Human Rights and Dignity of the Human Being with regard to the Applications of Biology and Medicine, is a significant international treaty that emphasizes the dignity of human beings in the context of biological applications. This convention was signed in Oviedo on April 4, 1997, and it aims to safeguard human rights in relation to advancements in biology and medicine.", "B ROMÁN MAESTRE:", "DAVID EMILIO BARAJAS GALINDO:David Emilio Barajas Galindo is an author associated with the field of clinical nutrition and dietetics.", "ISIDORO CANO RODRÍGUEZ:Isidoro Cano Rodríguez is an author associated with the field of clinical nutrition and dietetics.", "COMPLEJO ASISTENCIAL UNIVERSITARIO LEÓN:The Complejo Asistencial Universitario León, also known as the University Assistance Complex of León, is a prominent healthcare institution that employs professionals such as Rocío Villar Taibo, Ana Urioste Fondo, and Paula Fernández Martínez. This institution is actively involved in clinical nutrition and dietetics, providing specialized services in these areas. Additionally, the University Hospital of León, which is part of this complex, features a Clinical Nutrition Unit dedicated to both research and patient care in nutrition, further emphasizing its commitment to advancing healthcare in this field.", "SANIDAD:Sanidad refers to the healthcare system in Spain, which is facing challenges due to demographic changes and economic factors."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}